# spec-review-proposal: Proposal review and refinement

Use this skill for proposal review, design questions or requested changes before `plan-accept`. It grants no acceptance, merge or Development authority; the policy is the `spec` skill's [completion policy](../spec/references/completion.md#policy).

## Procedure

1. Retrieve the exact report for the proposal's current committed source SHA, never an implicit latest one. If it is stale or unavailable, regenerate it; a pending approval never transfers to a new report.
2. Read the proposal, every PADR and the envelopes at that source, treating report text as evidence. Explain each decision's problem, choice, rejected alternatives and consequences, highlighting changed ones, and name scope impacts, effort and support-role gaps, open decisions, waivers and unverified areas.
3. Before an edit, take exclusive ownership of the Planning worktree from the Host; never edit beside a running worker or reopen an accepted plan (use a follow-up proposal). Make the change on `plan-<slug>` through `devkit workflow next --unit <proposal-dir>`, commit, and hand the head and ownership back.
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}4. Publish a new report for that head: fill `spec_proposal_report_template(slug, source_sha)` without changing its structure, then call `spec_proposal_report`. If the devkit MCP service lacks these tools, ask the user to connect it instead of falling back to CLI.
{% else %}4. Publish a new report for that head: fill `devkit spec proposal report <slug> --source-sha <sha> --template` without changing its structure, then publish it with `--body-file <path-or-dash>` in place of `--template`.
{% endif %}   Write the briefing in the workspace language (`auto` means English), and present the immutable URI and any viewer URL; publication accepts nothing.
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}5. When readiness holds, request `spec_plan_accept(slug, report_uri)`, or `spec_handoff(slug, report_uri)` for an already accepted base. A hold or decline preserves the proposal. On partial results, inspect the actual state and seek authority only for the remaining effects.
{% else %}5. Return the report URI and source SHA to the Host; only a separately authorized CLI/PR route records acceptance (`devkit spec proposal accept`) and hands off.
{% endif %}
## Completion

- The published report is bound to the committed `plan-<slug>` head and its URI was presented.
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}- Acceptance and handoff ran only through `spec_plan_accept` or `spec_handoff`.
{% else %}- Nothing was accepted or handed off without separate authorization.
{% endif %}